{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he did not rinse his hands in water.</b> It would have appeared to us that any food and things like it that the zav touched—and the touching is with his hands and his hands are rinsed—is not impure, because he did not touch at the place of the flow, but rather as we saw all our ancestors interpreted 'and his hands' like 'his body,' we have accepted their words. And according to the plain sense: any pure thing that the zav touches, if his hands are rinsed, it becomes impure but not his garments; and if they were not rinsed, his garments become impure. This is like one who touches everything that is under him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:17.644358424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}